  "worked_solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}=b$, then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{2} \\\\ -3{x}_{2} \\\\ 5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}=-3 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying the first equation by $2$ and adding the resulting equations, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =-5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we substitute into the second equation to get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}-3(-5) & =1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1} & =-14 \\\\ {x}_{1} & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute ${x}_{1}=7$ and ${x}_{2}=-5$ into the third equation and obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}=-4 \\\\ 3(7)+5(-5) & =-4 \\\\ -4 & =-4,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives a true statement. \n\nSo the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=7$ and ${x}_{2}=-5,$ which means\n\n$$\n7{a}_{1}-5{a}_{2}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=7+(-5)=2.\n$$",
